      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Macarthur Charles et al.\n\nsymptoms of tuberculosis, a chest ra-\ndiograph suggestive of tuberculosis and\na response to tuberculosis therapy.\n\nParticipants aged 13-15 years were\ntreated in the paediatric clinic; those 16\nyears or older were treated in the adult\nclinic, and pregnant patients of any\nage received treatment in the obstetric\nclinic. Patients were seen by a physician\nevery 2 weeks during the first 3 months\nof therapy and by a nurse every month\nthereafter. Patients with symptoms or\nsigns of sexually transmitted infections\nwere provided with treatment, and free\ncondoms were offered at e",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the clinical care and follow-up of the Haitian adolescents and young adults on antiretroviral therapy, including clinic assignment by age and pregnancy, visit schedules, management of sexually transmitted infections and adherence support. It also explains laboratory methods, including viral load testing and resistance gene sequencing for specimens above 1000 copies/ml.",
