      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Macarthur Charles et al.\n\nHIV-1 drug resistance mutations\n\nAt 12 months of follow-up, 32 partici-\npants had > 1000 copies/ml of plasma\nHIV-1 RNA, and 29 patients’ plasma\nsamples could be amplified to yield a\nsequence. All clustered with clade B\nHIV-1. Table 2 summarizes the HIV-1\ndrug resistance mutations.\n\nTuberculosis\nOf the 146 patients starting ART, 27\n\n(18%) received concurrent treatment\nfor tuberculosis. Of these 27 patients,\n15 (56%) successfully completed anti-\ntuberculosis therapy, 6 (22%) had\ntherapeutic failure, 2 (7%) were lost to\nfollow-up, 3 (11%) died, and 1 (4%)\ncompleted thera",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Reports drug resistance mutations among 29 sequenced samples from Haitian youth with high viral loads at 12 months, all of clade B, and outcomes for those also treated for tuberculosis. It describes sexual activity, low condom use and pregnancies in the cohort, and suggests that the many mutations seen point to prolonged virological failure.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
